 A repository ruleset for the default branch (`main`):
 
-- Changes go in through a pull request with 1 approval. A new push dismisses earlier approvals, and
-  every review thread must be resolved.
+- Changes go in through a pull request with 1 approval, and that approval must come from a code
+  owner of the changed files (see below). A new push dismisses earlier approvals, and every review
+  thread must be resolved.
 - Both CI jobs must pass, on a branch that is up to date with `main`.
 - No force pushes and no deleting `main`.
 - Squash and merge commits are allowed. Nobody can bypass the rules, admins included.
 
+## Code owners (`.github/CODEOWNERS`)
+
+Each area of the repository has two owners. GitHub requests their review automatically when a pull
+request changes their files, and the ruleset requires one of them to approve. A pull request that
+changes several areas, such as `development` into `main`, needs an approval from an owner of each.
+
+| Area                                       | Owners                            |
+| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------- |
+| Everything not listed below                | @avaz-io, @BahadurNUU             |
+| `apps/api`                                 | @BahadurNUU, @nozimjonfribble     |
+| `apps/api/prisma` (schema and migrations)  | @nozimjonfribble, @dilnuraliqulov |
+| `apps/api/src/email`                       | @AlijonTursunboyev, @BahadurNUU   |
+| `apps/web`                                 | @BahadurNUU, @dilnuraliqulov      |
+| `apps/web/src/i18n` (en, uz, ru)           | @dilnuraliqulov, @nozimjonfribble |
+| `packages/shared`                          | @BahadurNUU, @dilnuraliqulov      |
+| `docs`                                     | @BahadurNUU, @nozimjonfribble     |
+| `.github`, `docs/ci.md`, Docker, toolchain | @avaz-io, @BahadurNUU             |
+
+Owners need write access to the repository (Settings → Collaborators). GitHub reads `CODEOWNERS`
+from the base branch of a pull request, so changes to it apply once they are merged into `main`.
+Open the file on GitHub to see any line it could not read.
+
 ### Turning it on
 
 The ruleset JSON does nothing until it is imported. It needs admin access to the repository.
